          "date": "2026-10-13 04:38:30.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20909 tests: fit sanity/42e to small OSTs and large pages",
        "message": "LU-20909 tests: fit sanity/42e to small OSTs and large pages\n\nsanity test_42e first writes max_dirty_mb to OST0000 and then dirties\nanother max_dirty_mb there, before writing 16-page files.  On small\ntest OSTs that already hold data from earlier subtests, the client\nruns out of grant and falls back to sync single-page writes, failing\nwith \"less than 16-pages write RPCs 39% > 15%\".  With PAGE_SIZE 16KiB\neach 16-page file is also 4x the size, which makes this much likelier.\n\nThe measured loop also continued the warmup loop's index, starting at\nOSTCOUNT * max_dirty_mb, so the number of files written depended on\nthe client RAM, and was zero with 4GiB or more of RAM, where the\nsubtest passed without checking anything.\n\nLimit max_dirty_mb to a quarter of the OST0000 free space for the\nsubtest, scale the number of files by 4096 / PAGE_SIZE so about 31MiB\nis written to OST0000 for any page size, start the measured loop at\n0, and fail if no file landed on OST0000.\n\nWith 40MiB already on a 400MiB OST0000, 16KiB-page aarch64 client:\n2/2 failed before (39%, 69% of RPCs under 16 pages), 4/4 pass after\nwith no RPC under 16 pages; 4KiB-page x86_64 client: 2/2 pass.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity env=ONLY=42e,ONLY_MINUTES=30 clientarch=aarch64 clientdistro=rocky9.8\nFixes: e817ad5b7557 (\"b=22074 block if grant is available or maybe available soon\")\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5.5 ltvm,llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Id2e236a33afef9f3eb801feff30a16478e3ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
